      "oldText": "META\n- SEO Title: Nansen CEO Warns AI Bubble to Burst as GPU Costs Drop—What It Means\n- Meta Description: Nansen CEO Alex Svanevik warns the AI infrastructure bubble is set to burst as GPU rental costs decline and Chinese models rise. Discover the implications for crypto and DePIN.\n- URL Slug: nansen-ceo-ai-bubble-burst-gpu-costs\n- Categories: AI, Latest News\n- Primary Keyword: Nansen CEO Warns\n- Secondary Keywords: AI bubble, GPU costs, DePIN, Chinese AI models",
      "newText": "META\n- SEO Title: Nansen CEO Warns AI Bubble to Burst as GPU Costs Drop\n- Meta Description: Nansen CEO Warns AI infrastructure bubble is bursting as GPU costs drop and Chinese models rise. Impact on crypto and DePIN projects.\n- URL Slug: nansen-ceo-ai-bubble-burst-gpu-costs\n- Categories: AI, Latest News\n- Primary Keyword: Nansen CEO Warns\n- Secondary Keywords: AI bubble, GPU costs, DePIN, Chinese AI models"
    },
    {
      "oldText": "# Nansen CEO Warns AI Bubble to Burst as GPU Costs Drop\n\nThe AI infrastructure bubble is on the verge of bursting, according to Alex Svanevik, CEO of on-chain analytics platform Nansen. In a stark assessment of the market as of June 20, 2026, Svanevik warned that declining GPU rental costs and the rise of efficient Chinese AI models are signaling a impending correction for the sector. His analysis, reported by [Cryptofox](https://cryptofox.news/news/nansen-ceo-warns-of-ai-bubble-burst-as-computing-costs-decline), suggests that the scarcity premium driving AI infrastructure valuations is evaporating, with ripple effects expected across both traditional tech and decentralized crypto projects. Meanwhile, [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2025/06/15/nvidia-gpu-shortage-eases-as-ai-chip-supply-increases/) highlights how increased supply and competition are easing the once-critical GPU shortage, further pressuring prices.",
      "newText": "# Nansen CEO Warns AI Bubble to Burst as GPU Costs Drop\n\nNansen CEO Warns the AI infrastructure bubble is bursting, with Alex Svanevik, CEO of on-chain analytics platform Nansen, highlighting declining GPU rental costs and the rise of efficient Chinese AI models as key triggers. His analysis, reported by [Cryptofox](https://cryptofox.news/news/nansen-ceo-warns-of-ai-bubble-burst-as-computing-costs-decline), suggests the scarcity premium driving AI infrastructure valuations is evaporating. This shift is poised to impact both traditional tech and decentralized crypto projects. Meanwhile, [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2025/06/15/nvidia-gpu-shortage-eases-as-ai-chip-supply-increases/) reports that increased supply and competition are easing the GPU shortage, further pressuring prices."
